+# Contract: Command-Line Interface
+
+**Feature**: `001-pastebin-service` | **Date**: 2026-11-16
+
+The operator-facing interface. The HTTP surface it exposes is defined in
+[http-api.md](./http-api.md).
+
+---
+
+## Invocation
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port PORT --data DIR
+```
+
+The package is `pastebin` under `src/`, runnable as `python -m pastebin` when `src/` is on
+`PYTHONPATH` (spec Constraints). `serve` is the only subcommand.
+
+### Arguments
+
+| Argument | Required | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `serve` | yes | subcommand | the only subcommand |
+| `--port` | yes | integer | 0 … 65535. `0` binds an ephemeral port and the **bound** port is reported |
+| `--data` | yes | path | data directory; created with parents if absent |
+
+**There is no `--host` flag.** The bind address is the fixed constant `127.0.0.1`; no option
+exposes the service on another interface (SR-011).
+
+---
+
+## Startup sequence
+
+In this order, so that the readiness line is never printed before the service can serve:
+
+1. Parse and validate arguments.
+2. Create the data directory with `mode=0o700` (including missing parents), then enforce `0700`
+   on it (FR-002, SR-008).
+3. Verify the directory is writable.
+4. Bind and listen on `127.0.0.1:<port>`.
+5. Print the readiness line to **stdout** and flush.
+6. Serve requests until interrupted.
+
+Because the listen backlog is open at step 4, a client that connects the instant it sees the
+readiness line is queued rather than refused (SC-006).
+
+---
+
+## Standard output
+
+On success, **stdout carries exactly one line and nothing else**:
+
+```text
+listening on 127.0.0.1:8080
+```
+
+- The port shown is the port actually bound. With `--port 0` this is the ephemeral port the
+  kernel chose, not `0` (FR-003).
+- Printed once, after binding, flushed immediately.
+- No request logging, no banners, no diagnostics are ever written to stdout — request logging is
+  suppressed entirely so that identifiers (which are capability URLs) are never recorded
+  (SR-009).
+
+---
+
+## Exit status
+
+| Status | Condition |
+|---|---|
+| `0` | Clean shutdown (`SIGINT` / `KeyboardInterrupt`) |
+| non-zero | Any startup failure (see below) |
+
+---
+
+## Startup failures
+
+Each prints a message to **stderr**, exits non-zero, and **does not print the readiness line**
+(FR-004).
+
+| Condition | Example stderr message |
+|---|---|
+| Missing/unparsable `--port` or `--data` | `argparse` usage error |
+| `--port` outside 0 … 65535 | `error: --port must be between 0 and 65535` |
+| Port already in use | `error: cannot bind 127.0.0.1:8080: address already in use` |
+| Data directory cannot be created | `error: cannot create data directory: <reason>` |
+| Data directory exists but is not writable | `error: data directory is not writable` |
+
+Failures are fatal — there is no fallback to another port, no fallback directory, and no
+best-guess coercion of an invalid argument (Constitution Principle II).
+
+Operator-facing stderr messages may name the port or directory the operator just supplied on the
+command line; this discloses nothing they do not already know. SR-009's redaction rule governs
+responses to network callers, which never contain a path.
+
+---
+
+## Shutdown
+
+`SIGINT` (Ctrl-C) stops the server cleanly and exits `0`. In-flight requests are allowed to
+complete. No cleanup of the data directory occurs — pastes are durable by design (FR-023).
+
+---
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+# Start on a fixed port
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port 8080 --data ./pastes-data
+# → listening on 127.0.0.1:8080
+
+# Start on an ephemeral port (useful in tests)
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port 0 --data /tmp/pb
+# → listening on 127.0.0.1:54321
+
+# Port already taken
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port 8080 --data ./pastes-data
+# stderr: error: cannot bind 127.0.0.1:8080: address already in use
+# exit status: 1, no readiness line on stdout
+```
