+# Contract: HTTP API
+
+**Feature**: `001-pastebin-service` | **Date**: 2026-11-16
+
+The caller-facing interface. All request and response bodies are JSON (`application/json;
+charset=utf-8`) **except** the raw-content response, which is `text/plain; charset=utf-8`.
+
+Base address: `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` — loopback only, no other interface is reachable
+(SR-011). Entity shapes are defined in [data-model.md](../data-model.md).
+
+---
+
+## Route table (closed)
+
+| Method | Path | Operation | Success |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `POST` | `/pastes` | Create a paste | `201` |
+| `GET` | `/pastes/<id>` | Read metadata + content | `200` |
+| `GET` | `/pastes/<id>/raw` | Read content as plain text | `200` |
+| `DELETE` | `/pastes/<id>` | Revoke a paste | `204` |
+
+**Every other request is `404`** with the standard error body — including unknown paths, a known
+path with an unsupported method (`GET /pastes`, `POST /pastes/<id>`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `HEAD`, …),
+an unknown sub-resource (`/pastes/<id>/anything`), and a trailing slash
+(`/pastes/<id>/`). There is no `405` and no `Allow` header (FR-028, spec Assumption
+"Unrecognised action on a known address returns not found").
+
+`<id>` must match `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}` exactly. Any other id segment — containing `/`, `..`, a
+percent-encoded separator, an absolute path, or of the wrong length — is `404`, and never reaches
+the filesystem (SR-003).
+
+---
+
+## Common response headers
+
+Present on every response:
+
+| Header | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `Content-Length` | exact byte length of the body (`0` for `204`) |
+| `Server` | `pastebin` — the default `BaseHTTP/x.y Python/z` banner is suppressed (SR-009) |
+
+No response — in any body, header, or log line — ever contains a `delete_token` (other than the
+single `201` that issues it), a filesystem path, or a stack trace (SR-009).
+
+---
+
+## Error body
+
+Every non-2xx response carries exactly:
+
+```json
+{"error": "<human-readable message>"}
+```
+
+with `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8` (FR-025). The message names the rule that
+was broken; it never echoes a stored value, an input value, a path, or internal state (SR-009).
+
+### Status codes used
+
+| Status | Meaning | Requirements |
+|---|---|---|
+| `400` | Malformed input — bad framing, undecodable/invalid JSON, non-object body, missing/non-string `content`, invalid `expires_in` | FR-026 |
+| `403` | Revocation of an existing, live paste with a missing or incorrect token | FR-020 |
+| `404` | Unknown or expired paste; unknown path; unsupported method on a known path | FR-028 |
+| `413` | `content` exceeds 65 536 encoded bytes, or the declared body size exceeds the cap | FR-027 |
+| `500` | Unexpected internal failure — generic message only, no content, no diagnostics | SR-010 |
+
+**Precedence rules**:
+1. `413` beats everything for an otherwise-valid oversized submission (FR-027).
+2. `404` beats `403` — non-existence is reported before a permission failure, for any id that is
+   unknown, expired, or already revoked, regardless of the token supplied (FR-021).
+
+---
+
+## `POST /pastes` — create
+
+### Request
+
+```http
+POST /pastes HTTP/1.1
+Host: 127.0.0.1:8080
+Content-Type: application/json
+Content-Length: 42
+
+{"content": "hello", "expires_in": 3600}
+```
+
+**Framing requirements** (checked before the body is read — SR-005, FR-029):
+
+- `Content-Length` MUST be present and a non-negative integer. Absent or malformed → `400`.
+- `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` is rejected → `400`.
+- `Content-Length` > `66560` (65 536 + 1 024 envelope slack) → `413`, **body not read**, response
+  carries `Connection: close`.
+- The body MUST deliver exactly `Content-Length` bytes; a short read → `400`.
+
+**Body fields**:
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Constraints |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `content` | string | yes | UTF-8; ≤ 65 536 encoded bytes; `""` is valid |
+| `expires_in` | integer | no | 1 … 2 592 000 seconds. `true`/`false`, floats, strings, and `null` are rejected. Absent ⇒ never expires |
+
+Any other field is ignored (FR-009). `Content-Type` is not enforced; the body is parsed as JSON
+regardless.
+
+### Response `201 Created`
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ",
+  "delete_token": "9rYQ0s3Xz2mKpLv8wTnB4jHcFdEaGuRi7NsOyPqZlMk",
+  "url": "/pastes/QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ"
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | string | 22 chars, `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, unique across all pastes ever issued (FR-011) |
+| `delete_token` | string | 43 chars. **Issued exactly once** — never returned by any read (FR-013) |
+| `url` | string | Relative address `/pastes/<id>` (FR-010) |
+
+### Failure cases
+
+| Condition | Status | Example message |
+|---|---|---|
+| Missing/invalid `Content-Length`, or chunked encoding | `400` | `"request must declare a valid Content-Length"` |
+| Declared size over the cap | `413` | `"content exceeds the maximum size of 65536 bytes"` |
+| Body shorter than declared | `400` | `"request body was shorter than the declared Content-Length"` |
+| Body is not valid UTF-8 | `400` | `"request body must be valid UTF-8"` |
+| Body is not valid JSON | `400` | `"request body must be a JSON object"` |
+| Body is a list/number/string/`null`/bool | `400` | `"request body must be a JSON object"` |
+| `content` missing | `400` | `"content is required"` |
+| `content` not a string | `400` | `"content must be a string"` |
+| `expires_in` not an integer (incl. `true`, `3600.0`, `"3600"`) | `400` | `"expires_in must be an integer between 1 and 2592000"` |
+| `expires_in` out of range (`0`, `-1`, `2592001`) | `400` | `"expires_in must be an integer between 1 and 2592000"` |
+| `content` over 65 536 encoded bytes | `413` | `"content exceeds the maximum size of 65536 bytes"` |
+
+---
+
+## `GET /pastes/<id>` — read metadata
+
+### Request
+
+```http
+GET /pastes/QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ HTTP/1.1
+Host: 127.0.0.1:8080
+```
+
+No headers or body are required; a body, if sent, is ignored.
+
+### Response `200 OK`
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ",
+  "content": "hello",
+  "created_at": "2026-11-16T09:41:07Z",
+  "expires_at": "2026-11-16T10:41:07Z"
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | string | the requested identifier |
+| `content` | string | exact original text — non-ASCII, emoji, newlines, quotes preserved (FR-016) |
+| `created_at` | string | ISO 8601 UTC, second precision, `Z` suffix (FR-015) |
+| `expires_at` | string \| null | same format, or `null` for a paste that never expires |
+
+`delete_token` is **never** present in this response (FR-013).
+
+### Failure cases
+
+| Condition | Status |
+|---|---|
+| Unknown id | `404` |
+| Expired paste | `404` |
+| Revoked paste | `404` |
+| Id failing the `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}` allowlist (traversal attempts, wrong length) | `404` |
+| Stored record corrupt or unparsable | `404` (FR-024) |
+
+Message: `"not found"`.
+
+---
+
+## `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` — read content as plain text
+
+### Request
+
+```http
+GET /pastes/QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ/raw HTTP/1.1
+Host: 127.0.0.1:8080
+```
+
+### Response `200 OK`
+
+```http
+HTTP/1.1 200 OK
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
+X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
+Content-Length: 5
+
+hello
+```
+
+- The body is `content.encode("utf-8")` **verbatim**: no trailing newline, no BOM, no quoting, no
+  JSON wrapper (FR-014).
+- `Content-Length` is the encoded byte count, so multi-byte text round-trips exactly (FR-016).
+- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` prevents a browser from sniffing the body as markup —
+  content is always inert (SR-012).
+- An empty paste returns a `200` with `Content-Length: 0` and an empty body.
+
+### Failure cases
+
+Identical to `GET /pastes/<id>` — `404` with the **JSON** error body (the error shape is JSON even
+though the success shape is plain text).
+
+---
+
+## `DELETE /pastes/<id>` — revoke
+
+### Request
+
+```http
+DELETE /pastes/QnJ3c2VyLVNhZmUtSWQ HTTP/1.1
+Host: 127.0.0.1:8080
+X-Delete-Token=[REDACTED:assigned_secret]
+```
+
+| Header | Required | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `X-Delete-Token` | yes | the secret issued in the `201` response |
+
+### Response `204 No Content`
+
+Empty body, `Content-Length: 0` (FR-019). Every subsequent read or revocation of that id is `404`
+(FR-022).
+
+### Failure cases — evaluation order matters
+
+The server evaluates in this exact order (FR-021):
+
+1. **Id fails the allowlist** → `404`
+2. **Record absent, corrupt, or expired** → `404` — *regardless of whether a token was supplied or
+   whether it was correct*
+3. **Token missing or incorrect** → `403`, and the paste remains readable with unchanged content
+   (FR-020)
+4. **Token correct** → `204`
+
+| Condition | Status | Message |
+|---|---|---|
+| Unknown id, with any token or none | `404` | `"not found"` |
+| Expired paste, with any token or none | `404` | `"not found"` |
+| Already-revoked paste, with the correct token | `404` | `"not found"` |
+| Live paste, `X-Delete-Token` absent | `403` | `"invalid delete token"` |
+| Live paste, wrong token | `403` | `"invalid delete token"` |
+
+The token is compared with `hmac.compare_digest` against the stored record on every request
+(SR-002, SR-006), inside the same lock as the removal (SR-007).
+
+**Concurrency**: two simultaneous correct revocations both succeed in the sense that the paste is
+removed; one receives `204` and the other `404`. No other error occurs.
+
+---
+
+## Behavioural invariants
+
+These hold across every route and are directly testable:
+
+1. **No secret leakage** — `delete_token` appears in exactly one response in the paste's lifetime:
+   the `201` that created it. No read, no error, no header, no log line contains it (FR-013,
+   SR-009).
+2. **No path leakage** — no response or log line contains a filesystem path or a stack trace
+   (SR-009, SR-010).
+3. **Exact round-trip** — for any `content` accepted at creation, both read forms return text byte
+   -identical to what was submitted (FR-016).
+4. **Expiry is absolute** — after `expires_at`, all three id-bearing routes return `404`. A paste
+   is readable *up to and including* its expiry instant (FR-017).
+5. **404 before 403** — the `403`/`404` distinction never reveals whether an id exists (FR-021).
+6. **Containment** — no request, however crafted, causes a read, write, or removal outside the
+   data directory (SR-003, SC-010).
+7. **Bounded memory** — the service never buffers more than ~66 KB from a single request
+   regardless of how much a caller attempts to send (FR-029, SR-005, SC-007).
+8. **Loopback only** — there is no configuration that binds any other interface (SR-011).
